      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "Οἱ δὲ ἐπιδεδωκότες τὰς ῥάβδους χλωράς, αὐτὰ δὲ τὰ ἄκρα ξηρὰ καὶ σχισμὰς ἔχοντα",
          "english_quote": "The people whose rods were green, with dry and cracked tips",
          "issue": "The simplified text omits the action of handing in the rods. The source identifies this group by the rods they submitted, not merely by rods they possessed. The same omission recurs in paragraph 3.",
          "suggested_revision": "Restore the submission action in both descriptions, for example: “The people who handed in green rods with dry and cracked tips” and “The people who handed in their dry rods with only a little green.”",
          "severity": "major"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ἀλλ᾿ ἀκούσαντές μου τῶν ῥημάτων τὸ πλεῖστον μέρος ταχὺ μετενόησαν",
          "english_quote": "Most heard my words and quickly repented.",
          "issue": "Moving “most” before “heard” changes its scope. The source presents hearing the speaker’s words as the circumstance preceding the majority’s quick repentance; the English instead quantifies who heard as well as who repented. It also drops the explicit contrast introduced by ἀλλ᾿.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider: “But after hearing my words, most of them quickly repented.”",
          "severity": "major"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "καὶ ἐγένετο ἡ κατοικία αὐτῶν εἰς τὸν πύργον.",
          "english_quote": "Their dwelling was in the tower.",
          "issue": "The static “was” loses the source’s assertion that their dwelling came to be in the tower following their repentance.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider: “And their dwelling came to be in the tower.”",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "τούτων οὖν πάντων ἡ κατοικία εἰς τὸν πύργον ἔσται.",
          "english_quote": "Retain both invited groups, the response conditions, suffering without supplied willingness, and the explicit Spirit/Son statement.",
          "issue": "The theological metadata claims that this unit contains an explicit Spirit/Son statement, which is absent from the selected source. Its references to both invited groups and response conditions likewise do not accurately describe this unit.",
          "suggested_revision": "Replace this metadata with a unit-specific explanation of the actual repentance assertions and bounded textual selections, without attributing a Spirit/Son statement to this section.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "τούτων οὖν πάντων ἡ κατοικία εἰς τὸν πύργον ἔσται.",
          "english_quote": "Retain rod fractions, both invited groups, repentance conditions, suffering without supplied willingness, the Spirit/Son identification and all twelve distinct mountain descriptions; preserve substantive alternative notes.",
          "issue": "The simplification metadata claims preservation of a Spirit/Son identification and twelve mountain descriptions, neither of which occurs in this source unit. This is an inaccurate description of what the supplied simplified edition translates.",
          "suggested_revision": "Rewrite the simplification record specifically for this section, documenting the rod descriptions, repentance language, negations, suffering reading, and substantive alternative notes. Remove claims about absent identifications and mountain descriptions.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The standard reader text covers the selected Greek faithfully, but its theological metadata requires correction. Independent review of the simplified text finds omitted rod-submission actions, altered scope in the hearing-and-repentance clause, and loss of the dwelling’s transition, alongside inaccurate metadata. Both editions follow the servant and contextual repentance policies. The disclosed only-believed and suffering selections should remain; the supplied reports do not justify replacing them merely because alternatives exist. This review evaluates the selected source and supplied disclosures, not unseen manuscripts or exhaustive collation. Proposed corrections require fresh review."
